  "id": "19",
  "name": "Manufacture of coke and refined petroleum products",
  "section": "C",
  "summary": "Refiners and coke producers describe AI in process control and optimisation (advanced process control, real-time optimisation, closed-loop AI, crude and blend optimisation), reliability (predictive maintenance, corrosion prediction, robotic inspection), safety and emissions monitoring, and trading and retail pricing. AI also appears as a market force: data-centre power demand, backup-generator fuel, immersion cooling fluids from lubricant businesses, and autonomous vehicles as a long-term fuel-demand risk. Cyber risk to operational technology and workforce knowledge capture are recurring themes; coke makers report intelligent coal blending and unmanned oven machinery.",
